 ## 1.0.0 (private, provisional)
 
+October 25 continuation: prevent replay after truncated acknowledgements or transport errors following a completed payload write; bound each HTTP request attempt by elapsed time, including socket queueing and trickling responses. Apply the existing sanitized error boundary to page, asset, Prometheus and stream admission failures before headers are sent. Enforce the Studio rate-limiter key bound for rejected clients. Add seven focused regressions and preserve all earlier repairs. Current exact-package and browser evidence is under readiness-2026-10-25.
+
+October 24 follow-up: prevent automatic HTTP replay after uncertain acknowledgement timeouts and after partial split acknowledgement; report delivery progress without claiming durable receipt. Complete health registration/report, metric discovery and synthetic removal declarations. Label the Studio operator token and authorization dialog. Preserve open trace/incident/diagnostic inspectors and active filters across automatic polling, with an explicit resume control. Fresh archive, browser and consumer evidence is under readiness-2026-10-24.
+
 Readiness hardening: sanitize Studio failures through the runtime serializer/redactor, cancel operator prompts without mutations, abort stale action ownership, and use CSP-compatible trace progress and labeled filters. Correct health/resource replacement identity, HTTP exporter terminal admission, JSONL initialization/drain accounting, trace ratio/context binding/baggage parsing, unmatched HTTP route labels, alert/notification callback lifecycle, delayed Redis subscription cleanup and finite fleet-envelope timestamps. Strengthen concrete envelope/span/tracer declarations and add an all-entrypoint strict type consumer. Preserve private metadata, unresolved license, ownership and publication rejection. Current archive verification and remaining acceptance gaps are recorded in the repository's readiness-2026-10-21 directory.
 
 Extracted the authoritative Monitor source and actual Studio frontend without modifying the app or sibling candidates. Added standalone exports, package-relative assets, injected provider policy, release guards, examples, native/adversarial tests and API/configuration evidence. Corrected lifecycle races, cancellation, stale subscriptions/series, bounded collector/exporter behavior, retention, durability acknowledgements, synthetic cleanup, untrusted body/envelope handling, redaction, and Studio mount/destroy behavior. See migration and validation documents for behavioral compatibility and remaining gaps.
